-- status  : Proved
-- author  : @Nickrobbins95
-- created : 2026-11-25T07:52:20.023719+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/0ab03020-45d8-4878-9d59-cbeb4c3e4b4d
-- title:
--   Kummer theory on a curve over $\overline{\mathbb F}_q$: $H^1(\bar X,\mu_N)\cong\{f:N\mid\operatorname{div}f\}/\bar F^{\times N}\;(=\operatorname{Pic}^0(\bar X)[N])$, Frobenius-equivariantly
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbb F_q$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$ and $F$ a function field in one variable over $\mathbb F_q$, separable over $\mathbb F_q(x)$, with $\mathbb F_q$ algebraically closed in $F$; let $X$ be the smooth projective curve with function field $F$. Let $A\subset F$ be the integral closure of $\mathbb F_q[x]$ (the coordinate ring of the affine part $U\subset X$) and $O_\infty\subset F$ the integral closure of the valuation ring of $\mathbb F_q(x)$ at $\infty$ (its maximal ideals are the points of $X$ over $\infty$). Let $N\ge1$ with $p\nmid N$. Inside an algebraic closure of $F$ let $F_m=F\cdot\mathbb F_{q^m}$ (generated by the roots of $T^{q^m}-T$) and $\bar F=\bigcup_mF_m=F\,\overline{\mathbb F}_q$, the function field of $\bar X=X\otimes\overline{\mathbb F}_q$. Let $K_U$ be the compositum of all finite Galois extensions $L/F$ in which every prime of the integral closure of $A$ in $L$ has trivial inertia group (the maximal extension unramified over $U$; it contains $\bar F$), and let $\Gamma\subseteq\operatorname{Gal}(K_U/F)$ be the subgroup fixing every $x$ with $x^{q^k}=x$ for some $k\ge1$, so $\Gamma=\operatorname{Gal}(K_U/\bar F)=\pi_1(\bar U)$ with its Krull topology. Put:
--
--   - $H$ = the locally constant homomorphisms $\chi:\Gamma\to K_U^\times$ with $\chi^N=1$ and $\chi(g)=1$ for every $g$ in the inertia group of every nonzero prime of the integral closure of $O_\infty$ in $K_U$ (every point of $\bar X$ over $\infty$). Since $\mu_N\subset\overline{\mathbb F}_q$ is fixed by $\Gamma$, $H=\operatorname{Hom}_{\rm cont}(\pi_1(\bar X),\mu_N)=H^1(\bar X,\mu_N)$;
--   - $D$ = the $f\in\bar F^\times$ with $N\mid\operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ of $F_m$, finite (a height-one prime of the integral closure of $A$ in $F_m$) or infinite (one of the integral closure of $O_\infty$ in $F_m$), for every $m$ with $f\in F_m$; i.e. $\operatorname{div}(f)\in N\operatorname{Div}(\bar X)$;
--   - $P=\bar F^{\times N}$, the $N$-th powers, a subgroup of $D$.
--
--   Then there is a group isomorphism
--   $$\Phi:H^1(\bar X,\mu_N)=H\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;D/P$$
--   given by Kummer theory: every $\chi\in H$ is a Kummer character, i.e. there is $\alpha\in K_U^\times$ with $g(\alpha)=\chi(g)\,\alpha$ for all $g\in\Gamma$, and for every such $\alpha$ one has $\alpha^N\in D$ and $\Phi(\chi)=[\alpha^N]$. Moreover $\Phi$ is Frobenius-equivariant: if $\varphi\in\operatorname{Gal}(K_U/F)$ acts on $\overline{\mathbb F}_q$ by $x\mapsto x^q$, $\chi,\chi'\in H$ satisfy $\chi'(\varphi g\varphi^{-1})=\varphi(\chi(g))$ for all $g\in\Gamma$, and $\Phi(\chi)=[f]$, then $\varphi(f)\in D$ and $\Phi(\chi')=[\varphi(f)]$.
--
--   Role: $f\mapsto\tfrac1N\operatorname{div}(f)$ identifies $D/P$ with $\operatorname{Pic}(\bar X)[N]=\operatorname{Pic}^0(\bar X)[N]$ (a function with trivial divisor is a constant in $\overline{\mathbb F}_q^\times$, hence an $N$-th power), so the theorem is the Kummer-sequence isomorphism $H^1(\bar X,\mu_N)\cong\operatorname{Pic}^0(\bar X)[N]$, equivalently $H^1(\bar X,\mathbb Z/N)\cong\operatorname{Pic}^0(\bar X)[N]\otimes\mu_N^{-1}$, compatible with Frobenius. With $N=\ell^n$ it identifies $H^1(\bar X,\mathbb Q_\ell)$ with the dual of the Tate module of the Jacobian, the input for computing Frobenius eigenvalues on $H^1$ of a curve. The statement uses this function model of $\operatorname{Pic}^0(\bar X)[N]$ rather than building $\operatorname{Pic}(\bar X)$ as a direct limit over the $F_m$. The proof: Hilbert 90 gives the radical $\alpha$; $\alpha^N$ is $\Gamma$-fixed, and unramifiedness of $F_m(\alpha)$ over $U$ and at $\infty$ is equivalent to $N\mid\operatorname{ord}_v(\alpha^N)$ for all $v$ (Kummer extensions of degree prime to $p$).
--
--   **Formalization Note**: `CL m` is $F_m$, `IntermediateField.adjoin F` of the roots of $T^{q^m}-T$ in `AlgebraicClosure F`; `hk : algebraicClosure Fq F = ⊥` says $\mathbb F_q$ is algebraically closed in $F$; `hN : (N : F) ≠ 0` says $N\ge1$ and $p\nmid N$. `KU` is the supremum of the finite-dimensional Galois intermediate fields $L$ in which no nontrivial $g\in\operatorname{Gal}(L/F)$ lies in the inertia group of a prime $P$ of `integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) L` (inertia written as $g(b)-b\in P$ for all $b$); `FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F` is $A$ and `integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F` is $O_\infty$. `Γ`, `H`, `D`, `P` are variables fixed uniquely by their membership conditions `hΓ`, `hH`, `hD`, `hP`; local constancy is for the Krull topology on `KU ≃ₐ[F] KU` restricted to `Γ`, and the inertia condition in `hH` ranges over all nonzero primes `Q` of `integralClosure (O_∞) KU`. In `hD` the orders are read off Mathlib's `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation` through `WithZero.log` (which gives $-\operatorname{ord}_v$, irrelevant for divisibility); the instances `IsDedekindDomain` and `IsFractionRing` for the integral closures in `CL m` are bound by `∀ [...]` (they always hold, `CL m` being finite separable over $F$), so these conditions simply range over all height-one primes. $\bar F^\times$ is represented by the units of `KU` fixed by `Γ`. The quotient is `D ⧸ P.subgroupOf D`, and $\varphi$ acts on units through `Units.map`. Example: for an elliptic function field and $N=\ell$ both sides are $(\mathbb Z/\ell)^2$; for $F=\mathbb F_q(x)$ both are trivial.
-- source:
--   J. S. Milne, Étale Cohomology, Princeton University Press (1980), Ch. III §4 (Kummer theory) and Ch. V §2; J. S. Milne, Lectures on Étale Cohomology, §13–14 ($H^1(X,\mu_n)$ and $\operatorname{Pic}(X)[n]$ for curves); M. Rosen, Number Theory in Function Fields, Springer GTM 210 (2002), Ch. 10 (Kummer extensions)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem FunctionField.geomH1_rootsOfUnity_equiv_divisibleDivisors_modPow
    (Fq : Type) [Field Fq] [Fintype Fq] [DecidableEq (RatFunc Fq)]
    (F : Type) [Field F] [Algebra Fq F] [Algebra (Polynomial Fq) F] [Algebra (RatFunc Fq) F]
    [IsScalarTower (Polynomial Fq) (RatFunc Fq) F] [IsScalarTower Fq (Polynomial Fq) F]
    [FunctionField Fq F] [Algebra.IsSeparable (RatFunc Fq) F]
    (hk : algebraicClosure Fq F = ⊥)
    (N : ℕ) (hN : (N : F) ≠ 0)
    (CL : ℕ → IntermediateField F (AlgebraicClosure F))
    (hCL : ∀ m, CL m = IntermediateField.adjoin F
      (((Polynomial.X : Polynomial F) ^ (Fintype.card Fq ^ m) - Polynomial.X).rootSet (AlgebraicClosure F)))
    (KU : IntermediateField F (AlgebraicClosure F))
    (hKU : KU = ⨆ L : {L : IntermediateField F (AlgebraicClosure F) //
        FiniteDimensional F L ∧ IsGalois F L ∧
        ∀ P : Ideal (integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) L), P.IsPrime →
          ∀ g : L ≃ₐ[F] L,
            (∀ b : integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) L, ∃ c ∈ P, (c : L) = g b - b) →
              g = 1}, L.1)
    (Γ : Subgroup (KU ≃ₐ[F] KU))
    (hΓ : ∀ g : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU, g ∈ Γ ↔
      ∀ x : KU, (∃ k : ℕ, 0 < k ∧ x ^ (Fintype.card Fq) ^ k = x) → g x = x)
    (H : Subgroup (Γ →* KUˣ))
    (hH : ∀ χ : Γ →* KUˣ, χ ∈ H ↔ IsLocallyConstant χ ∧ (∀ g : Γ, χ g ^ N = 1) ∧
      ∀ Q : Ideal (integralClosure (integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F) KU),
        Q.IsPrime → Q ≠ ⊥ → ∀ g : Γ,
          (∀ b : integralClosure (integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F) KU,
            ∃ c ∈ Q, (c : KU) = (g : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU) b - b) → χ g = 1)
    (D : Subgroup KUˣ)
    (hD : ∀ f : KUˣ, f ∈ D ↔ (∀ g ∈ Γ, g (f : KU) = f) ∧
      ∀ m : ℕ, 0 < m → ∀ hm : ((f : KU) : AlgebraicClosure F) ∈ CL m,
        (∀ [IsDedekindDomain (integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) (CL m))]
          [IsFractionRing (integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) (CL m)) (CL m)]
          (v : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (integralClosure (FunctionField.ringOfIntegers Fq F) (CL m))),
          (N : ℤ) ∣ WithZero.log (v.valuation (CL m) ⟨_, hm⟩)) ∧
        (∀ [IsDedekindDomain (integralClosure
            (integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F) (CL m))]
          [IsFractionRing (integralClosure
            (integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F) (CL m)) (CL m)]
          (w : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (integralClosure
            (integralClosure (RatFunc.inftyValuation Fq).valuationSubring F) (CL m))),
          (N : ℤ) ∣ WithZero.log (w.valuation (CL m) ⟨_, hm⟩)))
    (P : Subgroup KUˣ)
    (hP : ∀ f : KUˣ, f ∈ P ↔ ∃ b : KUˣ, (∀ g ∈ Γ, g (b : KU) = b) ∧ f = b ^ N) :
    ∃ Φ : H ≃* D ⧸ P.subgroupOf D,
      (∀ χ ∈ H, ∃ α : KUˣ, ∀ g : Γ, (g : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU) α = (χ g : KU) * α) ∧
      (∀ (χ : H) (α : KUˣ), (∀ g : Γ, (g : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU) α = ((χ : Γ →* KUˣ) g : KU) * α) →
        ∃ hα : α ^ N ∈ D, Φ χ = QuotientGroup.mk (⟨α ^ N, hα⟩ : D)) ∧
      ∀ φ : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU,
        (∀ x : KU, (∃ k : ℕ, 0 < k ∧ x ^ (Fintype.card Fq) ^ k = x) → φ x = x ^ Fintype.card Fq) →
        ∀ (χ χ' : H) (f : D),
          (∀ g g' : Γ, (g' : KU ≃ₐ[F] KU) = φ * g * φ⁻¹ →
            (((χ' : Γ →* KUˣ) g' : KUˣ) : KU) = φ (((χ : Γ →* KUˣ) g : KUˣ) : KU)) →
          Φ χ = QuotientGroup.mk f →
          ∃ hf : Units.map (φ : KU →* KU) (f : KUˣ) ∈ D,
            Φ χ' = QuotientGroup.mk (⟨Units.map (φ : KU →* KU) (f : KUˣ), hf⟩ : D) := by
